    "text": "A long cylindrical conductor of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;is made of a material whose resistivity depends only on the distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> from the axis of the conductor as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math> is a constant. The resistance of the conductor across the two ends will be",
